## Logo

### Primary wordmark
- Typeface: Pinyon Script
- Title case, natural letter-spacing
- Used on hero placements, splash screens, pitch decks, and signage
- The script wordmark is the face of the brand. It should feel handwritten, personal, like a signature.

### Caps wordmark (secondary)
- Typeface: Playfair Display, 400 weight
- All caps, letter-spacing 0.18em
- Used when the script is too delicate for the context (small sizes, dark busy backgrounds, footer text)

### Monogram
- Single letterform "D" in Pinyon Script
- Used for app icon, favicon, watermarks, compact brand marks
- Always paired with the wordmark in small type below when space allows

### Logo clear space
- Minimum clear space around any logo mark: 1x the cap height of the wordmark on all sides
- Never place the logo on busy photography or patterned backgrounds without a solid backing surface

### Logo dont's
- Never stretch, rotate, or outline the wordmark
- Never use the gold on a yellow or orange background
- Never set the tagline in a typeface other than Cormorant Garamond

