| Warm white | #FAF8F5 | Primary background, cards, surfaces |
| Rich black | #1A1714 | Primary text, dark mode background, monogram |
| Muted gold | #C4A265 | Primary accent, CTAs, interactive highlights |
| Warm stone | #8A7D6B | Secondary text, captions, metadata |
| Sand | #E8DED0 | Dividers, subtle fills, secondary backgrounds |

### Extended palette

| Name | Hex | Usage |
|------|-----|-------|
| Cream | #F5F0E8 | Card backgrounds on warm white surfaces |
| Terracotta | #B87A56 | Seasonal accent, editorial highlights |
| Soft sage | #A8B09A | Success states, positive feedback |
| Mist | #D4D0C8 | Disabled states, placeholder text |
| Deep espresso | #2C2520 | Dark mode elevated surfaces |

### Colour rules
- Gold is never used as a background fill for large areas. It is an accent only.
- Warm white (#FAF8F5) is preferred over pure white (#FFFFFF). Pure white feels clinical and breaks the warmth.
- On dark backgrounds, use gold (#C4A265) for headings and warm white (#FAF8F5) for body text. Never use pure white on dark.
- Text on gold buttons: Rich black (#1A1714), never white.
- Minimum contrast ratio: 4.5:1 for body text, 3:1 for large text and UI components.

