## Typography

### Typeface system

| Role | Typeface | Weight | Size | Tracking |
|------|----------|--------|------|----------|
| Logo / Signature | Pinyon Script | 400 | 40-64px | 0 |
| Display / Caps alternate | Playfair Display | 400 | 32-48px | 0.18em |
| Editorial headings | Cormorant Garamond | 300, 400 | 24-36px | 0.04em |
| Body text | Inter or system sans | 400 | 14-16px | 0 |
| Captions / metadata | Inter or system sans | 400 | 11-13px | 0.02em |
| Buttons / labels | Inter or system sans | 500 | 13-14px | 0.04em |

### Typography rules
- The Pinyon Script wordmark is a signature, not a typeface for general use. It appears only as the logo and monogram. Never set body text, headings, or UI labels in Pinyon Script.
- Headings are always serif. Body is always sans-serif. Never reverse this.
- Cormorant Garamond at 300 weight is the signature of the brand. It should feel like it is barely there.
- Avoid bold weights on serif text. The brand voice is quiet confidence, not volume.
- Line height for body text: 1.6 to 1.7. Line height for headings: 1.2.
- Paragraph width should not exceed 65 characters for readability.

