## Photography and Imagery

### Style
- Warm, natural lighting. Mediterranean warmth preferred over studio harshness.
- Full-body or three-quarter shots. Outfit is the subject, not the face.
- Backgrounds: warm neutrals, architecture, natural textures (stone, linen, sand).
- No stark white studio backgrounds. No neon. No heavy post-processing.

### Colour grading
- Slight warm shift: pull shadows toward amber, highlights toward cream.
- Desaturate by 10-15%. Drape imagery should never look hyperreal.
- Black point: lift slightly (never crush to true black).

### Composition
- Generous negative space. At least 30% of the frame should be empty.
- Subject off-centre where possible. Editorial, not catalogue.
- When showing outfits, every piece should be identifiable. No cropping shoes or accessories unless intentional.

